course: dictionary
lesson: 3961
title: Furry: soft and fur-like
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Furry means covered with fur, or soft and thick like fur. Fur is the warm, soft hair that covers many animals. You can say a cat is furry, and you can also say a toy or a hat is furry if it feels like fur.
explain: Read the words around it to be sure. «On a cold spring morning a fat furry bumblebee queen is often the first bee out.» The word furry sits next to bumblebee, so it describes the bee's soft, hairy body. Try the swap: a fat hairy bumblebee queen still makes sense, so furry means hairy and soft here.
explain: Furry can also describe a coating that looks like fur. A furry tongue or furry mould is not made of real hair, but it looks like a soft, fuzzy layer. The word is about how something looks and feels, not always about an animal.
fact: Furry means covered with fur, or soft and thick like fur.
fact: Furry animals are mammals with fur that keeps them warm.
fact: Everyday furry things include pets, teddy bears, slippers and hats.
fact: «Furry friend» and «a furry toy» are common phrases; furry often makes things sound soft and cuddly.
fact: Furry is an adjective, and its comparative forms are furrier and furriest.
exercise: «On a cold spring morning a fat furry bumblebee queen is often the first bee out.» What does furry mean here? | Bright yellow and striped | Fast and buzzing | Very cold and icy | *Covered in soft, thick hair
exercise: «Every evening she lies across Sam's bedroom door like a furry draught excluder.» Why might a draught excluder be called furry? | It is made of glass | It makes a loud noise | It stops the rain | *It is soft and thick, like fur
exercise: Find and copy the word in «covered in soft furry velvet» that describes a fur-like texture. | velvet | *furry | full | dries
test: «A furry friend» most likely means | A friend who lives under the sea | A friend who is always cold | A friend who sings loudly | *A pet covered in soft fur
test: Furry can describe a coating. What does furry mean in «a furry tongue»? | Long and thin | Very clean and shiny | Full of water | *A coating that looks like fur
exam: «The horse chestnut's sticky buds burst open, and a huge furry queen bumblebee zigzags low over the lawn.» What does furry tell you about the queen bumblebee? | She is tiny and green | She is dangerous and fast | *She is soft and covered in fur | She is hungry
